Promise.any() takes an iterable of promises and returns a Promise that fulfills when ANY promise fulfills. Only rejects if ALL promises reject, with an AggregateError.

Syntax: Promise.any(iterable)

Return: First fulfillment value, ignoring rejections until a fulfillment is found.

Best for: Trying multiple fallback sources, using whichever succeeds first.

Example:
```javascript
const pErr = new Promise((resolve, reject) => reject(new Error('Always fails')));
const pSlow = new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 500, 'Done eventually'));
const pFast = new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 100, 'Done quick'));

Promise.any([pErr, pSlow, pFast]).then((value) => console.log(value));
// 'Done quick'

// All reject → AggregateError
Promise.any([Promise.reject(new Error('fail'))]).catch((err) => console.log(err));
// AggregateError: No Promise in Promise.any was resolved
```

Real-world: Fetch first available image from multiple CDNs, use whichever responds first.

