```javascript
async function parallelExample() {
  const [x, y] = await Promise.all([
    resolveAfter2Seconds(10),
    resolveAfter2Seconds(20),
  ]);
  // Total: ~2 seconds
}
```

Concurrency interleaving — await yields control to other async tasks:
```javascript
async function foo(name) {
  console.log(name, 'start');
  await console.log(name, 'middle');
  console.log(name, 'end');
}
foo('First');
foo('Second');
// First start → First middle → Second start → Second middle → First end → Second end
```

Key rule: Use Promise.all() when operations are independent; use sequential await only when second depends on first result.

