An async function declaration creates a function that always returns a Promise. The await keyword is permitted within the body.

Syntax: async function name(params) { statements }

Return behavior: Non-promise return values are implicitly wrapped in Promise.resolve().

Example:
```javascript
async function foo() { return 1; }
// Equivalent to:
function foo() { return Promise.resolve(1); }
```

Execution flow:
1. Top-level code runs synchronously up to first await
2. At await: execution suspends, control returns to caller
3. After promise resolves: control re-enters function

Error handling:
