Web Workers run scripts in background OS-level threads without blocking the main thread. The main thread and worker communicate via postMessage() — data is copied (structured clone), not shared by default.

Types:
- Dedicated Workers: single script only
- Shared Workers: multiple scripts/windows
- Service Workers: proxy/cache for PWA

Creation:
```javascript
const worker = new Worker('./generate.js');
```

Main thread sending to worker:
```javascript
worker.postMessage({ command: 'generate', quota: 1000000 });
worker.addEventListener('message', (message) => {
  console.log('Result:', message.data);
});
worker.onerror = (error) => console.log(`Error: ${error.message}`);
```

Worker receiving and responding:
```javascript
addeventListener('message', (message) => {
  if (message.data.command === 'generate') {
    const result = heavyComputation(message.data.quota);
    postMessage(result);
  }
});
```

Worker termination:
```javascript
worker.terminate(); // immediately kills the worker
```

Data transfer options:
1. Structured clone (copy) — default, safe
2. Transferable objects (zero-copy, ownership moves):
```javascript
const uInt8Array = new Uint8Array(1024 * 1024 * 32);
worker.postMessage(uInt8Array.buffer, [uInt8Array.buffer]);
// uInt8Array.buffer is now empty in main thread
```
3. SharedArrayBuffer — shared memory, both sides read/write same bytes

Workers CANNOT access: DOM, window object, document.
Workers CAN access: fetch(), setTimeout(), WebSockets, IndexedDB.

