**Scenario (E-commerce):** Implementing this pattern to handle products efficiently.

Problem: synchronous CPU-heavy task blocks main thread and freezes UI. Solution: offload to Worker.

BAD (blocks UI):
```javascript
document.querySelector('#generate').addEventListener('click', () => {
  const quota = document.querySelector('#quota').value;
  const primes = generatePrimes(quota); // page freezes here
  document.querySelector('#output').textContent = `Finished generating ${quota} primes!`;
});
```

GOOD (non-blocking with Worker):

Main thread (main.js):
```javascript
const worker = new Worker('./generate.js');
document.querySelector('#generate').addEventListener('click', () => {
  const quota = document.querySelector('#quota').value;
  worker.postMessage({ command: 'generate', quota });
});
worker.addEventListener('message', (message) => {
  document.querySelector('#output').textContent =
    `Finished generating ${message.data} primes!`;
});
```

Worker (generate.js):
```javascript
addEventListener('message', (message) => {
  if (message.data.command === 'generate') {
    generatePrimes(message.data.quota);
  }
});
function generatePrimes(quota) {
  // heavy computation...
  postMessage(primes.length); // send result back
}
```

Key insight: Worker runs on separate OS thread. Main thread remains fully responsive to user interactions during computation.

