A floating promise is a promise that is created but not returned from a .then() handler. The chain loses track of it, causing race conditions and lost data.

BAD — floating promise (missing return):
```javascript
doSomething()
  .then((url) => {
    fetch(url); // NOT returned! This is a floating promise
  })
  .then((result) => {
    // result is undefined — fetch result is lost
  });
```

BAD — race condition from floating promise:
```javascript
const listOfIngredients = [];
doSomething()
  .then((url) => {
    fetch(url) // missing return
      .then((res) => res.json())
      .then((data) => { listOfIngredients.push(data); });
  })
  .then(() => {
    console.log(listOfIngredients); // always [] — fetch hasn't completed
  });
```

GOOD — return the promise:
```javascript
doSomething()
  .then((url) => {
    return fetch(url); // returned
  })
  .then((result) => {
    // result is the Response object
  });
```

GOOD — flat chain (even better):
```javascript
doSomething()
  .then((url) => fetch(url))
  .then((res) => res.json())
  .then((data) => { listOfIngredients.push(data); })
  .then(() => console.log(listOfIngredients));
```

Fix: Always return promises from .then() handlers. Use eslint rule: no-floating-promises.

