**Scenario (E-commerce):** Implementing this pattern to handle products efficiently.

Multiple concurrent async operations writing to the same object or array without coordination causes unpredictable final state.

PROBLEM:
```javascript
const results = [];

async function fetchAndStore(url) {
  const data = await fetch(url).then(r => r.json());
  results.push(data); // concurrent pushes — order is non-deterministic
}

await Promise.all([
  fetchAndStore('/api/1'),
  fetchAndStore('/api/2'),
  fetchAndStore('/api/3'),
]);
// results order is random: could be [3,1,2], [2,3,1], etc.
```

PROBLEM — shared counter:
```javascript
let total = 0;
async function addAmount(amount) {
  const current = total; // stale read
  await someAsyncWork();
  total = current + amount; // overwrites concurrent writes
}
await Promise.all([addAmount(10), addAmount(20)]);
// total may be 10 or 20 instead of 30
```

FIX — collect results from Promise.all directly:
```javascript
const results = await Promise.all([
  fetch('/api/1').then(r => r.json()),
  fetch('/api/2').then(r => r.json()),
  fetch('/api/3').then(r => r.json()),
]);
// results order matches input order — deterministic
```

FIX — accumulate after all complete:
```javascript
const amounts = await Promise.all([fetchAmount(1), fetchAmount(2)]);
const total = amounts.reduce((sum, x) => sum + x, 0);
```

