**Scenario (E-commerce):** Implementing this pattern to handle products efficiently.

Synchronous CPU-intensive operations on the main thread block the event loop — no async callbacks, timers, or I/O can run until the blocking code finishes.

PROBLEM — synchronous heavy computation:
```javascript
app.get('/api/compute', (req, res) => {
  // This blocks ALL other requests for the duration
  const result = expensiveComputation(req.body.data); // may take seconds
  res.json(result);
});

// While compute runs:
// - other HTTP requests are queued
// - timers don't fire
// - database callbacks don't run
```

PROBLEM — JSON.parse on large payload:
```javascript
const data = JSON.parse(hugeJsonString); // synchronous, blocks event loop
```

FIX — offload to Worker Thread (Node.js):
```javascript
const { Worker, isMainThread, parentPort, workerData } = require('worker_threads');

if (isMainThread) {
  app.get('/api/compute', (req, res) => {
    const worker = new Worker(__filename, { workerData: req.body.data });
    worker.on('message', (result) => res.json(result));
    worker.on('error', (err) => res.status(500).json({ error: err.message }));
  });
} else {
  const result = expensiveComputation(workerData); // runs in worker thread
  parentPort.postMessage(result);
}
```

FIX — split work with setImmediate to yield to event loop:
```javascript
async function chunkedComputation(items) {
  const results = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
    results.push(process(items[i]));
    if (i % 100 === 0) {
      await new Promise((resolve) => setImmediate(resolve)); // yield
    }
  }
  return results;
}
```

