structuredClone() creates a deep clone using the structured clone algorithm. Supports circular references. Can optionally transfer (move) objects rather than copying them.

Deep clone — independent copy:
```javascript
const original = { name: 'MDN', nested: { value: 42 } };
original.itself = original; // circular reference

const clone = structuredClone(original);

clone.nested.value = 99;
console.log(original.nested.value); // 42 — unaffected
console.log(clone.itself === clone); // true — circular preserved
```

Transfer (zero-copy move — original becomes detached):
```javascript
const buffer = new ArrayBuffer(1024 * 1024 * 32); // 32MB
const transferred = structuredClone(buffer, { transfer: [buffer] });

console.log(buffer.byteLength); // 0 — original emptied
console.log(transferred.byteLength); // 33554432 — moved
```

Use transfer before async operations to prevent accidental modification:
```javascript
async function processBuffer(rawBuffer) {
  // Transfer ownership — caller can no longer modify rawBuffer
  const safeBuffer = structuredClone(rawBuffer, { transfer: [rawBuffer] });
  await validate(safeBuffer);
  return transform(safeBuffer);
}
```

Supported: primitives, objects, arrays, Date, Map, Set, TypedArrays, ArrayBuffers, Blobs, ImageData, circular refs. Unsupported: functions, DOM nodes, WeakMap (throws DataCloneError).

