ReadableStream represents a readable source of byte data. Enables processing data in chunks without loading everything into memory. Core of the Streams API.

Async iteration (simplest):
```javascript
const response = await fetch('https://example.org/large-file');
let totalBytes = 0;

for await (const chunk of response.body) {
  totalBytes += chunk.length;
  process(chunk);
}
console.log('Total:', totalBytes);
```

Custom ReadableStream:
```javascript
const stream = new ReadableStream({
  start(controller) {
    controller.enqueue('Hello ');
    controller.enqueue('world');
    controller.close();
  }
});
```

Piping — chain streams:
```javascript
const response = await fetch(url);
const decoded = response.body
  .pipeThrough(new TextDecoderStream()) // bytes → strings
  .pipeTo(writable); // destination sink
```

Tee — split one stream into two:
```javascript
const [branch1, branch2] = response.body.tee();
// Both branches get identical data
await Promise.all([
  branch1.pipeTo(cacheStore),
  branch2.pipeTo(uiRenderer)
]);
```

From async generator:
```javascript
const myStream = ReadableStream.from(async function*() {
  yield 'first';
  await delay(100);
  yield 'second';
}());
```

Key: once a reader is acquired via getReader(), stream is locked — no other reader until released. Cancel stops consumption.

