Async generator functions (async function*) return AsyncGenerator objects that implement both async iterable and async iterator protocols. Each yield implicitly wraps the value in a Promise.

Basic:
```javascript
async function* delayedNumbers() {
  yield await fetch('/api/first').then(r => r.json());
  yield await fetch('/api/second').then(r => r.json());
  yield 42; // non-promise auto-wrapped
}

const gen = delayedNumbers();
await gen.next(); // { value: <first result>, done: false }
await gen.next(); // { value: <second result>, done: false }
await gen.next(); // { value: 42, done: false }
await gen.next(); // { value: undefined, done: true }
```

With for-await-of:
```javascript
async function* generate() {
  yield new Promise(r => setTimeout(() => r(1), 2000));
  yield new Promise(r => setTimeout(() => r(2), 1000));
  yield 3;
}

for await (const value of generate()) {
  console.log(value); // 1, 2, 3 (in order, despite different delays)
}
```

Error handling in async generators:
```javascript
