Web Workers run JavaScript in a separate thread — true concurrency for CPU-bound work without blocking the UI thread. Communication via message passing (data is copied, not shared).

Spawn and communicate:
```javascript
// main.js
const worker = new Worker('worker.js');

worker.postMessage({ task: 'compute', data: largeArray });

worker.onmessage = (e) => {
  console.log('Result:', e.data.result);
};

worker.onerror = (err) => {
  console.error(`Error in ${err.filename}:${err.lineno}`, err.message);
};

// Stop worker
worker.terminate();
```

```javascript
// worker.js
onmessage = (e) => {
  const { task, data } = e.data;
  if (task === 'compute') {
    const result = expensiveComputation(data);
    postMessage({ result });
  }
};
```

Transferable objects — zero-copy transfer:
```javascript
const buffer = new ArrayBuffer(1024 * 1024 * 64); // 64MB
worker.postMessage(buffer, [buffer]); // transfer — main loses access
// buffer.byteLength === 0 after transfer
```

Worker limitations: no DOM, no window object (use self). Can use fetch, setTimeout, IndexedDB, WebSockets, importScripts().

Feature detect:
```javascript
if (window.Worker) {
  const worker = new Worker('worker.js');
}
```

