Fetch is Promise-based HTTP client. Combine with Promise.all for concurrent requests, AbortController for cancellation, ReadableStream for streaming.

Concurrent fetches:
```javascript
// All start simultaneously — total time ≈ slowest single request
const [users, products, orders] = await Promise.all([
  fetch('/api/users').then(r => r.json()),
  fetch('/api/products').then(r => r.json()),
  fetch('/api/orders').then(r => r.json()),
]);
```

Retry with exponential backoff:
```javascript
async function fetchWithRetry(url, options = {}, retries = 3) {
  for (let attempt = 0; attempt < retries; attempt++) {
    try {
      const res = await fetch(url, options);
      if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`);
      return await res.json();
    } catch (err) {
      if (attempt === retries - 1) throw err;
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 2 ** attempt * 1000));
    }
  }
}
```

Cancellable with timeout:
```javascript
async function fetchWithTimeout(url, ms = 5000) {
  const res = await fetch(url, { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(ms) });
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`);
  return res.json();
}
```

Streaming response (process as data arrives):
```javascript
async function streamJSON(url) {
  const res = await fetch(url);
  for await (const chunk of res.body.pipeThrough(new TextDecoderStream())) {
    processChunk(chunk);
  }
}
```

Key: response.body is a ReadableStream — readable only once. Clone response to read multiple times: const clone = response.clone().

