TransformStream bridges a WritableStream and ReadableStream — data written to the writable side is transformed and available on the readable side. Used for format conversion, encoding, compression in streaming pipelines.

Built-in TransformStream: TextDecoderStream, TextEncoderStream:
```javascript
const response = await fetch('/api/text-data');
for await (const text of response.body.pipeThrough(new TextDecoderStream())) {
  console.log(text);
}
```

Custom transform:
```javascript
const uppercaseTransform = new TransformStream({
  transform(chunk, controller) {
    controller.enqueue(chunk.toUpperCase());
  },
  flush(controller) {
    // Called when writable side closes
    controller.terminate();
  }
});

const { readable, writable } = uppercaseTransform;

// Pipe: source → transform → destination
fetch('/api/data')
  .then(res => res.body)
  .then(body => body
    .pipeThrough(new TextDecoderStream())
    .pipeThrough(uppercaseTransform)
    .pipeTo(outputWritable)
  );
```

Chain multiple transforms:
```javascript
readableSource
  .pipeThrough(new TextDecoderStream())
  .pipeThrough(new TransformStream({ transform(chunk, ctrl) {
    ctrl.enqueue(JSON.parse(chunk));
  }}))
  .pipeTo(dataProcessor);
```

TransformStream is transferable — can be sent between workers via postMessage.

