WritableStream is the destination (sink) in a Streams API pipeline. Accepts data written via a writer or piped from a ReadableStream. Includes built-in backpressure.

Writer pattern:
```javascript
const logStream = new WritableStream({
  write(chunk) {
    logEl.textContent += chunk + '\n';
  },
  close() {
    console.log('Stream closed');
  },
  abort(reason) {
    console.error('Stream aborted:', reason);
  }
});

const writer = logStream.getWriter();
await writer.write('First line');
await writer.write('Second line');
await writer.close();
```

Pipe from ReadableStream:
```javascript
const response = await fetch('/api/data');
await response.body
  .pipeThrough(new TextDecoderStream())
  .pipeTo(logStream);
```

Backpressure — getWriter().ready is a Promise that resolves when stream can accept more data:
```javascript
const writer = writableStream.getWriter();

for (const chunk of chunks) {
  await writer.ready; // wait if buffer is full
  await writer.write(chunk);
}
await writer.close();
```

Locking: getWriter() locks the stream — only one writer at a time. Release with writer.releaseLock(). Abort stream: writer.abort(reason) or stream.abort(reason) — discards queued writes and moves to error state.

