Backpressure — getWriter().ready is a Promise that resolves when stream can accept more data:
```javascript
const writer = writableStream.getWriter();

for (const chunk of chunks) {
  await writer.ready; // wait if buffer is full
  await writer.write(chunk);
}
await writer.close();
```

Locking: getWriter() locks the stream — only one writer at a time. Release with writer.releaseLock(). Abort stream: writer.abort(reason) or stream.abort(reason) — discards queued writes and moves to error state.

