MessagePort is one end of a MessageChannel pipe. Transferable — can be moved between workers via postMessage. Enables point-to-point communication between any two contexts.

```javascript
// Create the channel
const { port1, port2 } = new MessageChannel();

// Set up port1 listener
port1.onmessage = (e) => console.log('port1 received:', e.data);

// Transfer port2 to a worker (zero-copy, port2 now owned by worker)
worker.postMessage({ type: 'SETUP' }, [port2]);

// Send to worker via port1
port1.postMessage({ data: 'hello worker' });
```

In worker:
```javascript
onmessage = (e) => {
  if (e.data.type === 'SETUP') {
    const workerPort = e.ports[0]; // received port2
    workerPort.onmessage = (msg) => {
      workerPort.postMessage({ reply: msg.data.data.toUpperCase() });
    };
    workerPort.start(); // required with addEventListener
  }
};
```

start() vs onmessage:
- `port.onmessage = handler` — implicitly calls start(), begins receiving
- `port.addEventListener('message', handler)` — requires explicit `port.start()`
- `port.close()` — disconnects port, no more messages

Use case: direct worker-to-worker communication (bypass main thread) by transferring ports.

