queueMicrotask(fn) schedules fn as a microtask — after current synchronous code but before the next macrotask (setTimeout/setInterval). Higher priority than setTimeout(fn, 0).

Execution order:
```javascript
console.log('sync 1');

setTimeout(() => console.log('macrotask'), 0);

Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log('microtask (promise)'));

queueMicrotask(() => console.log('microtask (explicit)'));

console.log('sync 2');

// Output: sync 1 → sync 2 → microtask (promise) → microtask (explicit) → macrotask
```

Use case — consistent async behavior (cache hit vs miss):
```javascript
function loadData(key) {
  if (cache.has(key)) {
    // Without queueMicrotask: sync callback, inconsistent with async path
    queueMicrotask(() => {
      callback(null, cache.get(key));
    });
  } else {
    fetchFromDB(key).then(data => {
      cache.set(key, data);
      callback(null, data);
    });
  }
}
```

Batch updates — coalesce multiple state changes:
```javascript
let pending = [];
let scheduled = false;

function scheduleUpdate(update) {
  pending.push(update);
  if (!scheduled) {
    scheduled = true;
    queueMicrotask(() => {
      applyUpdates(pending.splice(0));
      scheduled = false;
    });
  }
}
```

CRITICAL PITFALL — infinite loop freezes browser:
```javascript
// NEVER do this:
function loop() { queueMicrotask(loop); } // browser hangs — microtask queue never empties
```

