SharedArrayBuffer is a fixed-size raw binary buffer shared across multiple Workers (no copy on postMessage). Requires cross-origin isolation for security (COOP/COEP headers).

Security headers required:
```
Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
```

Basic shared memory:
```javascript
// Main thread
const sab = new SharedArrayBuffer(1024); // 1KB shared
const arr = new Int32Array(sab);

worker.postMessage({ buffer: sab }); // sent by reference, not copy

// Check availability
if (!crossOriginIsolated) {
  console.warn('SharedArrayBuffer not available — need COOP/COEP headers');
}
```

In worker:
```javascript
onmessage = (e) => {
  const arr = new Int32Array(e.data.buffer); // same memory
  Atomics.add(arr, 0, 1); // thread-safe increment
};
```

Parallel computation with shared results array:
```javascript
const resultBuffer = new SharedArrayBuffer(4 * 4); // 4 ints
const results = new Int32Array(resultBuffer);

const workers = Array.from({ length: 4 }, (_, i) => {
  const w = new Worker('./compute-worker.js');
  w.postMessage({ buffer: resultBuffer, index: i, range: [i*250, (i+1)*250] });
  return w;
});
```

Growable SharedArrayBuffer:
```javascript
const sab = new SharedArrayBuffer(1024, { maxByteLength: 4096 });
sab.grow(2048); // expand — can only grow, never shrink
```

Without Atomics, changes from one thread may not be visible to others or may be reordered.

