**Scenario (E-commerce):** Implementing this pattern to handle products efficiently.

Multiple async operations that write to shared state without coordination produce non-deterministic results.

PROBLEM — concurrent counter increment:
```javascript
let counter = 0;

async function increment() {
  const current = counter;        // read
  await delay(Math.random() * 10); // simulate async work
  counter = current + 1;          // write with stale value
}

await Promise.all([increment(), increment(), increment()]);
console.log(counter); // likely 1, not 3 — reads all got 0
```

PROBLEM — concurrent array push:
```javascript
const results = [];
await Promise.all(
  items.map(async (item) => {
    const processed = await process(item);
    results.push(processed); // concurrent pushes — order undefined
  })
);
// results.length may be correct but order is non-deterministic
```

FIX 1 — collect then assign:
```javascript
const results = await Promise.all(items.map(process)); // order preserved
```

FIX 2 — sequential when truly dependent:
```javascript
for (const item of items) {
  const result = await process(item);
  results.push(result);
}
