**Scenario (E-commerce):** Implementing this pattern to handle products efficiently.

Array.forEach does not await async callbacks — all iterations fire concurrently and forEach returns before any complete. The surrounding await does nothing.

PROBLEM:
```javascript
async function processAll(items) {
  items.forEach(async (item) => {
    await saveToDatabase(item); // awaited inside callback
  });
  // forEach returns immediately — none of the saves are done yet
  console.log('done'); // prints BEFORE any save completes
}

await processAll(items); // awaiting a void function — no guarantee
```

PROBLEM — concurrent writes may violate ordering:
```javascript
const results = [];
items.forEach(async (item) => {
  const result = await process(item);
  results.push(result); // non-deterministic order
});
```

FIX 1 — Promise.all + map (concurrent, results in order):
```javascript
const results = await Promise.all(items.map(async (item) => {
  return await process(item);
}));
```

FIX 2 — for-of (sequential):
```javascript
const results = [];
for (const item of items) {
  results.push(await process(item)); // sequential, awaited
}
```

FIX 3 — for-of with concurrency limit:
```javascript
async function processWithLimit(items, limit) {
  const semaphore = new Array(limit).fill(Promise.resolve());
  let i = 0;
  return Promise.all(items.map(item => {
    const index = i++ % limit;
    return semaphore[index] = semaphore[index].then(() => process(item));
  }));
}
```

Rule: forEach is synchronous iteration — never use async callbacks with it. Use for-of (sequential) or Promise.all + map (concurrent).

