Retry failed async operations with increasing delays — prevents thundering herd on temporarily unavailable services.

```javascript
async function withRetry(fn, options = {}) {
  const {
    maxAttempts = 3,
    baseDelay = 1000,
    maxDelay = 30000,
    onRetry = () => {},
  } = options;

  let lastError;

  for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= maxAttempts; attempt++) {
    try {
      return await fn();
    } catch (err) {
      lastError = err;
      if (attempt === maxAttempts) break;

      const delay = Math.min(baseDelay * 2 ** (attempt - 1), maxDelay);
      const jitter = Math.random() * delay * 0.1; // 10% jitter
      onRetry({ attempt, delay, error: err });
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, delay + jitter));
    }
  }

  throw lastError;
}
```

Usage:
```javascript
const data = await withRetry(
  () => fetch('/api/flaky-endpoint').then(r => r.json()),
  {
    maxAttempts: 5,
    baseDelay: 500,
    onRetry: ({ attempt, error }) => console.warn(`Attempt ${attempt} failed:`, error),
  }
);
```

With AbortSignal support:
```javascript
async function withRetry(fn, { signal, ...opts } = {}) {
  for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= opts.maxAttempts; attempt++) {
    signal?.throwIfAborted();
    try {
      return await fn({ signal });
    } catch (err) {
      if (err.name === 'AbortError') throw err; // don't retry abort
      // ... delay and retry
    }
  }
}
```

Jitter prevents thundering herd: all failed clients retry at different times instead of simultaneously.

