**Scenario (E-commerce):** Implementing this pattern to handle products efficiently.

Use performance.mark() and performance.measure() to measure precise duration of async operations — better than Date.now() (high-resolution timestamps, DevTools integration).

Basic measurement:
```javascript
performance.mark('fetch-start');
const data = await fetch('/api/data').then(r => r.json());
performance.mark('fetch-end');

const measure = performance.measure('fetch-duration', 'fetch-start', 'fetch-end');
console.log(`Fetch took ${measure.duration.toFixed(2)}ms`);
```

Measure concurrent operations:
```javascript
performance.mark('parallel-start');

const [users, orders] = await Promise.all([
  fetch('/api/users').then(r => r.json()),
  fetch('/api/orders').then(r => r.json()),
]);

performance.mark('parallel-end');
performance.measure('parallel-fetch', 'parallel-start', 'parallel-end');

const [seq] = performance.getEntriesByName('parallel-fetch');
console.log(`Parallel fetch: ${seq.duration.toFixed(2)}ms`);
```

Observe all measures passively:
```javascript
const observer = new PerformanceObserver((list) => {
  list.getEntries().forEach(entry => {
    if (entry.entryType === 'measure') {
      console.log(`${entry.name}: ${entry.duration.toFixed(2)}ms`);
    }
  });
});
observer.observe({ entryTypes: ['measure', 'mark'] });
```

Cleanup:
```javascript
performance.clearMarks();
performance.clearMeasures('fetch-duration');
```

Detail metadata (attach arbitrary data to a mark):
```javascript
performance.mark('worker-result', { detail: { itemCount: results.length } });
```

