Web Locks API provides named locks that work across tabs, workers, and contexts of the same origin. Lock is held while an async callback runs; automatically released on completion.

Basic exclusive lock:
```javascript
navigator.locks.request('my_resource', async (lock) => {
  // Only one tab/worker runs this at a time
  await syncDataToServer();
  await updateLocalCache();
  // Lock released when function returns
});
```

Await the lock:
```javascript
await navigator.locks.request('db_sync', async (lock) => {
  const data = await fetchFromRemote();
  await writeToIndexedDB(data);
});
// Lock released — continues here
```

Shared (readers-writer) lock:
```javascript
// Multiple readers simultaneously
await navigator.locks.request('cache', { mode: 'shared' }, async () => {
  return cache.read();
});

// Exclusive writer blocks all readers
await navigator.locks.request('cache', { mode: 'exclusive' }, async () => {
  await cache.write(newData);
});
```

With timeout (AbortSignal):
```javascript
const controller = new AbortController();
const timeout = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 5000);

try {
  await navigator.locks.request(
    'resource',
    { signal: controller.signal },
    async (lock) => { await doWork(); }
  );
} catch (err) {
  if (err.name === 'AbortError') console.error('Lock timeout');
} finally {
  clearTimeout(timeout);
}
```

Query state:
```javascript
const { held, pending } = await navigator.locks.query();
console.log('Held locks:', held.map(l => l.name));
```

