IndexedDB is the browser's async database. All operations are event-driven and wrapped in transactions. Concurrency: multiple readonly transactions can run simultaneously; only one readwrite transaction per object store at a time.

Open database:
```javascript
const request = indexedDB.open('MyDB', 1);

request.onupgradeneeded = (e) => {
  const db = e.target.result;
  db.createObjectStore('users', { keyPath: 'id' });
};

request.onsuccess = (e) => {
  const db = e.target.result;
  // use db
};
```

Promise wrapper (recommended pattern):
```javascript
function idbRequest(req) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    req.onsuccess = () => resolve(req.result);
    req.onerror = () => reject(req.error);
  });
}

async function getUser(db, id) {
  const tx = db.transaction('users', 'readonly');
  const store = tx.objectStore('users');
  return idbRequest(store.get(id));
}
```

Transaction lifetime — do NOT return to event loop mid-transaction:
```javascript
// WRONG: await inside transaction kills it
const tx = db.transaction('users', 'readwrite');
const user = await fetch('/api/user').then(r => r.json()); // event loop returned
tx.objectStore('users').put(user); // TRANSACTION_INACTIVE_ERR

// CORRECT: fetch first, then start transaction
const user = await fetch('/api/user').then(r => r.json());
const tx2 = db.transaction('users', 'readwrite');
tx2.objectStore('users').put(user);
```

Concurrent readonly (fine):
```javascript
// Both run simultaneously
const [tx1, tx2] = [
  db.transaction('users', 'readonly'),
  db.transaction('orders', 'readonly'),
];
```

