scheduler.postTask() schedules tasks with explicit priority levels. Higher-priority tasks preempt lower-priority ones in the task queue. Alternative to setTimeout() with priority awareness.

Three priority levels:
- `user-blocking` — critical UI responses (highest)
- `user-visible` — default, visible updates
- `background` — non-urgent work (lowest)

```javascript
// Background task — runs after user-visible work
scheduler.postTask(() => {
  syncAnalytics();
}, { priority: 'background' });

// User-visible task — runs before background
scheduler.postTask(() => {
  updateUI(newData);
}, { priority: 'user-visible' });

// User-blocking — runs first
scheduler.postTask(() => {
  respondToClick();
}, { priority: 'user-blocking' });
// Execution order: user-blocking → user-visible → background
```

With async/await:
```javascript
const result = await scheduler.postTask(
  async () => {
    const data = await fetchData();
    return processData(data);
  },
  { priority: 'user-visible', delay: 100 }
);
```

Cancellable with TaskController:
```javascript
const controller = new TaskController({ priority: 'background' });

scheduler.postTask(longRunningTask, { signal: controller.signal })
  .catch(err => {
    if (err.name === 'AbortError') console.log('Task cancelled');
  });

// Change priority dynamically
controller.setPriority('user-blocking');

// Cancel
controller.abort();
```

Feature detect:
```javascript
if ('scheduler' in globalThis) {
  scheduler.postTask(task);
} else {
  setTimeout(task, 0); // fallback
}
```

