CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing) controls which cross-origin fetch requests browsers allow. Affects concurrent API calls to different origins.

Simple request (no preflight) — GET/POST with standard headers:
```javascript
const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/data');
// Server needs: Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * (or specific origin)
```

Preflight (OPTIONS sent automatically for PUT/DELETE/custom headers):
```javascript
const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/data', {
  method: 'PUT',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'X-Custom': 'value' },
  body: JSON.stringify(data)
});
// Browser sends OPTIONS first — server must respond:
// Access-Control-Allow-Methods: PUT
// Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Content-Type, X-Custom
```

Concurrent cross-origin requests — each triggers own preflight:
```javascript
// 6 requests → 6 preflights if CORS not cached
const results = await Promise.all([
  fetch('https://api-a.com/users'),
  fetch('https://api-a.com/orders'),  // same origin as above → shared preflight cache
  fetch('https://api-b.com/products'), // different origin → separate preflight
]);
// Server can cache preflight via Access-Control-Max-Age: 86400
```

With credentials (cookies/auth):
```javascript
const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/profile', {
  credentials: 'include', // send cookies
});
// Server must: Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true
// AND:         Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://myapp.com (NOT *)
```

OPAQUE response (no-cors mode) — cannot read body but can cache:
```javascript
fetch('https://other-origin.com/image.png', { mode: 'no-cors' });
```

