**Scenario (E-commerce):** Implementing this pattern to handle products efficiently.

Lazy singleton initialization without coordination causes the resource to be created multiple times when multiple callers trigger initialization concurrently.

PROBLEM:
```javascript
let db = null;

async function getDatabase() {
  if (!db) {
    // Race: multiple callers all pass the null check simultaneously
    db = await openDatabaseConnection(); // all create separate connections
  }
  return db;
}

// Concurrent callers
const [a, b, c] = await Promise.all([
  getDatabase(),
  getDatabase(), // db still null when this runs
  getDatabase(), // db still null when this runs
]);
// Three connections opened — a !== b !== c
```

FIX — store the promise, not the result:
```javascript
let dbPromise = null;

function getDatabase() {
  if (!dbPromise) {
    // Promise stored immediately — concurrent callers share it
    dbPromise = openDatabaseConnection();
  }
  return dbPromise; // all callers await same promise
}

const [a, b, c] = await Promise.all([
  getDatabase(),
  getDatabase(), // same promise
  getDatabase(), // same promise
]);
// a === b === c — one connection
```

FIX — with reset on failure:
```javascript
let dbPromise = null;

function getDatabase() {
  if (!dbPromise) {
    dbPromise = openDatabaseConnection()
      .catch(err => {
        dbPromise = null; // allow retry on failure
        throw err;
      });
  }
  return dbPromise;
}
```

