**Scenario (E-commerce):** Implementing this pattern to handle products efficiently.

Optimistic UI updates apply changes immediately, then sync with server. Concurrent updates without version control cause conflicts — server has one value, UI shows another, no merge strategy.

PROBLEM:
```javascript
// User A and User B both edit the same record simultaneously
async function saveTitle(newTitle) {
  // Optimistic update — show immediately
  document.title = newTitle;
  document.getElementById('title').textContent = newTitle;

  // Async save — may conflict with other saves
  const response = await fetch('/api/document/1', {
    method: 'PUT',
    body: JSON.stringify({ title: newTitle }),
  });
  // No conflict detection — last write wins silently
}
```

FIX — optimistic concurrency with version (ETag):
```javascript
let version = null;

async function loadDocument() {
  const res = await fetch('/api/document/1');
  version = res.headers.get('ETag');
  return res.json();
}

async function saveTitle(newTitle) {
  // Optimistic update
  renderTitle(newTitle);

  try {
    const res = await fetch('/api/document/1', {
      method: 'PUT',
      headers: {
        'Content-Type': 'application/json',
        'If-Match': version, // only update if version matches
      },
      body: JSON.stringify({ title: newTitle }),
    });

    if (res.status === 412) { // Precondition Failed
      // Conflict — reload and show merge UI
      const latest = await loadDocument();
      showConflictDialog(newTitle, latest.title);
    } else {
      version = res.headers.get('ETag');
    }
  } catch (err) {
    revertTitle(); // undo optimistic update
    throw err;
  }
}
```

