crypto.randomUUID() generates a cryptographically secure v4 UUID. Used to create idempotency keys — unique per-request identifiers that allow safe retry without duplicate processing.

```javascript
const uuid = crypto.randomUUID();
// '36b8f84d-df4e-4d49-b662-bcde71a8764f'
```

Idempotency key pattern:
```javascript
async function submitOrder(orderData) {
  const idempotencyKey = crypto.randomUUID();

  // Even if this runs twice (retry, double-click), server only processes once
  const response = await fetchWithRetry('/api/orders', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      'Idempotency-Key': idempotencyKey,
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(orderData),
  });

  return response.json();
}
```

Request deduplication with UUID:
```javascript
const pendingRequests = new Map();

async function deduplicatedFetch(url, options = {}) {
  const key = url + JSON.stringify(options.body ?? '');

  if (pendingRequests.has(key)) {
    return pendingRequests.get(key); // reuse in-flight request
  }

  const requestId = crypto.randomUUID();
  const promise = fetch(url, {
    ...options,
    headers: { ...options.headers, 'X-Request-ID': requestId }
  }).finally(() => pendingRequests.delete(key));

  pendingRequests.set(key, promise);
  return promise;
}
```

Available in Web Workers. Requires secure context (HTTPS). No parameters — always returns a fresh UUID. Cryptographically random — no guessing, safe for security-sensitive deduplication.

