MessageChannel creates a direct communication port between two workers, bypassing the main thread. Reduces latency and avoids bottlenecking the main thread for worker-to-worker data.

Main thread: create channel, give each worker one port:
```javascript
const { port1, port2 } = new MessageChannel();

const workerA = new Worker('./worker-a.js');
const workerB = new Worker('./worker-b.js');

// Transfer ports — main thread loses access after transfer
workerA.postMessage({ type: 'SETUP', role: 'sender' }, [port1]);
workerB.postMessage({ type: 'SETUP', role: 'receiver' }, [port2]);
```

Worker A (sender):
```javascript
let channel;
onmessage = (e) => {
  if (e.data.type === 'SETUP') {
    channel = e.ports[0];
    // Send data directly to Worker B
    channel.postMessage({ data: computeResult() });
  }
};
```

Worker B (receiver):
```javascript
let channel;
onmessage = (e) => {
  if (e.data.type === 'SETUP') {
    channel = e.ports[0];
    channel.onmessage = (msg) => {
      processData(msg.data.data);
      channel.postMessage({ ack: true }); // bidirectional
    };
    channel.start();
  }
};
```

Close when done:
```javascript
channel.close();
```

Use case: pipeline workers — Worker A produces, Worker B consumes — direct channel avoids round-trip through main thread for every message.

