**Scenario (E-commerce):** Implementing this pattern to handle products efficiently.

Try multiple data sources in order — primary, secondary, local cache — returning the first successful result. Concurrent optional fallbacks.

Sequential fallback chain:
```javascript
async function getDataWithFallback(id) {
  const sources = [
    () => fetchFromPrimaryAPI(id),
    () => fetchFromSecondaryAPI(id),
    () => fetchFromLocalCache(id),
    () => getDefaultData(id),
  ];

  for (const source of sources) {
    try {
      const result = await source();
      if (result) return result;
    } catch {
      // try next source
    }
  }

  throw new Error('All data sources failed');
}
```

Promise.any — fastest successful source wins:
```javascript
async function getRacingFallback(id) {
  try {
    return await Promise.any([
      fetchFromCDN1(id),
      fetchFromCDN2(id),
      fetchFromCDN3(id),
    ]);
  } catch (agg) {
    // AggregateError — all failed
    return getDefaultData(id);
  }
}
```

Race with timeout fallback:
```javascript
async function getWithTimeout(id, ms = 2000) {
  try {
    return await Promise.race([
      fetchData(id),
      new Promise((_, reject) => setTimeout(() => reject(new Error('timeout')), ms))
    ]);
  } catch {
    return getCachedData(id) ?? getDefaultData(id);
  }
}
```

