Very long async functions that do not yield control prevent other microtasks from running, starve lower-priority tasks, and make cancellation impossible mid-execution.

PROBLEM — no cancellation point:
```javascript
async function processMillionItems(items) {
  const results = [];
  for (const item of items) {
    // No await — never yields. If signal.aborted, no way to check
    results.push(heavyTransform(item));
  }
  return results;
  // Entire 1M iterations run without yielding — blocks microtask queue
}
```

FIX — periodic yield + cancellation check:
```javascript
async function processMillionItems(items, signal) {
  const results = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
    signal?.throwIfAborted(); // check cancellation

    results.push(heavyTransform(items[i]));

    // Yield every 1000 items — allow other tasks to run
    if (i % 1000 === 0) {
      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 0)); // macrotask yield
    }
  }
  return results;
}
```

FIX — scheduler.postTask for yielding with priority:
```javascript
async function processWithYield(items, signal) {
  const results = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
    signal?.throwIfAborted();
    results.push(heavyTransform(items[i]));

    if (i % 500 === 0 && 'scheduler' in globalThis) {
      await scheduler.postTask(() => {}, { priority: 'user-visible' });
    }
  }
  return results;
}
```

Rule: Long CPU loops in async code must yield periodically. No loop should run for more than ~50ms without a yield point.

