Choosing the right Promise concurrency method depends on failure tolerance and which-wins semantics.

| Method | Resolves when | Rejects when | Result shape |
|--------|------------|------------|-------------|
| Promise.all | ALL fulfilled | FIRST rejection | Array of values |
| Promise.allSettled | ALL settled | Never | Array of {status, value/reason} |
| Promise.race | FIRST settled | FIRST rejected (if first) | Single value |
| Promise.any | FIRST fulfilled | ALL rejected | Single value |

Use case matrix:
```javascript
// All must succeed (strict) — form validation
const [user, perms] = await Promise.all([validateUser(), validatePerms()]);

// Partial failure OK — dashboard widgets
const results = await Promise.allSettled([
  fetchWeather(), fetchNews(), fetchStocks()
]);
results.forEach(r => r.status === 'fulfilled' && renderWidget(r.value));

// Timeout pattern — race vs timer
const data = await Promise.race([
  fetchData(),
  new Promise((_, r) => setTimeout(() => r(new Error('timeout')), 5000))
]);

// Fallback CDN — first to respond
const image = await Promise.any([
  fetch('https://cdn1.example.com/img.png'),
  fetch('https://cdn2.example.com/img.png'),
  fetch('https://cdn3.example.com/img.png'),
]);
```

AggregateError (from Promise.any when all reject):
```javascript
try {
  await Promise.any([Promise.reject(new Error('A')), Promise.reject(new Error('B'))]);
} catch (err) {
  console.log(err instanceof AggregateError); // true
  console.log(err.errors); // [Error: A, Error: B]
}
```

