Web Workers run in WorkerGlobalScope — a different global than window. No DOM access, but rich API set for async/network operations.

Available in workers (use via self or direct):
```javascript
// worker.js

// Load external scripts synchronously
importScripts('lib1.js', 'lib2.js');

// self = WorkerGlobalScope (like window in main thread)
console.log(self.location.href); // worker script URL
console.log(self.navigator.userAgent);

// Timing
const id = setTimeout(() => {}, 1000);
const ivId = setInterval(() => {}, 500);
clearTimeout(id);
clearInterval(ivId);

// Async scheduling
queueMicrotask(() => { /* runs before next event */ });

// Network
const res = await fetch('/api/data');
const data = await res.json();

// Crypto
const uuid = crypto.randomUUID();
const random = new Uint32Array(8);
crypto.getRandomValues(random);

// Storage (async)
const db = indexedDB.open('MyDB', 1);
const cache = await caches.open('v1');

// Deep clone
const copy = structuredClone(complexObject);

// Performance
performance.mark('work-start');
```

NOT available in workers:
- document, window, alert, confirm
- localStorage, sessionStorage
- DOM manipulation APIs

Receive/send messages:
```javascript
self.onmessage = (e) => {
  const result = compute(e.data);
  self.postMessage(result);
};

self.onerror = (e) => {
  console.error('Worker error:', e.message);
};

self.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (e) => {
  console.error('Unhandled rejection in worker:', e.reason);
});
```

