**Scenario (E-commerce):** Implementing this pattern to handle products efficiently.

In frameworks like React, components unmount while async operations are still in flight — setState on unmounted component, or stale closures updating wrong component instance.

PROBLEM — setState after unmount:
```javascript
// React-style component
function UserProfile({ userId }) {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    async function load() {
      const data = await fetchUser(userId);
      setUser(data); // may run after component unmounts
    }
    load();
  }, [userId]);
}
// Warning: Can't perform a React state update on an unmounted component
```

FIX — cleanup flag:
```javascript
useEffect(() => {
  let cancelled = false;

  async function load() {
    const data = await fetchUser(userId);
    if (!cancelled) setUser(data);
  }
  load();

  return () => { cancelled = true; }; // cleanup on unmount
}, [userId]);
```

FIX — AbortController:
```javascript
useEffect(() => {
  const controller = new AbortController();

  fetch(`/api/users/${userId}`, { signal: controller.signal })
    .then(r => r.json())
    .then(data => setUser(data))
    .catch(err => {
      if (err.name !== 'AbortError') setError(err);
    });

  return () => controller.abort(); // cancels fetch on unmount/userId change
}, [userId]);
```

FIX — stale userId check (for non-fetch async):
```javascript
useEffect(() => {
  const currentUserId = userId;
  processUser(userId).then(result => {
    if (currentUserId === userId) setUser(result); // still same user
  });
}, [userId]);
```

