**Scenario (E-commerce):** Implementing this pattern to handle products efficiently.

User navigates away before async data loading completes — load finishes and updates UI/state for a route that is no longer active.

PROBLEM (SPA navigation):
```javascript
router.on('navigate', async (path) => {
  const data = await fetchPageData(path); // 2 seconds
  // User navigated to different page while fetching
  renderPage(path, data); // renders wrong page over current
});
```

FIX — route version counter:
```javascript
let currentRoute = null;
let routeVersion = 0;

router.on('navigate', async (path) => {
  const version = ++routeVersion;
  currentRoute = path;

  const data = await fetchPageData(path);

  if (version !== routeVersion) return; // stale — user has moved on
  renderPage(path, data);
});
```

FIX — AbortController per navigation:
```javascript
let navController = null;

router.on('navigate', async (path) => {
  navController?.abort(); // cancel previous navigation load
  navController = new AbortController();

  try {
    const data = await fetchPageData(path, { signal: navController.signal });
    renderPage(path, data);
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.name !== 'AbortError') renderError(err);
  }
});
```

FIX — structured scope:
```javascript
router.on('navigate', async (path) => {
  await withScope(async (scope) => {
    const data = await scope.spawn(sig =>
      fetchPageData(path, { signal: sig })
    );
    renderPage(path, data);
  }); // scope auto-cancels if navigate fires again
});
```

