WebTransport enables low-latency bidirectional communication using HTTP/3, supporting reliable streams and unreliable datagrams. Available in secure contexts and Web Workers.

Connection lifecycle:
```javascript
async function initTransport(url) {
  const transport = new WebTransport(url); // e.g. 'https://example.com:4999/wt'
  await transport.ready; // wait for QUIC handshake
  console.log('Transport ready');

  transport.closed.then(() => {
    console.log('Closed gracefully');
  }).catch((err) => {
    console.error('Closed with error:', err);
  });

  return transport;
}
```

Bidirectional streams (full duplex):
```javascript
async function sendAndReceive(transport, data) {
  const stream = await transport.createBidirectionalStream();
  const writer = stream.writable.getWriter();
  const reader = stream.readable.getReader();

  await writer.write(new TextEncoder().encode(data));
  await writer.close();

  const { value } = await reader.read();
  return new TextDecoder().decode(value);
}
```

Unidirectional streams (send-only):
```javascript
async function sendMessage(transport, message) {
  const stream = await transport.createUnidirectionalStream();
  const writer = stream.getWriter();
  await writer.write(new TextEncoder().encode(message));
  await writer.close();
}
```

Unreliable datagrams for real-time data (low latency, may be dropped):
```javascript
async function sendDatagram(transport, data) {
  const writer = transport.datagrams.writable.getWriter();
  await writer.write(data);
}

async function receiveDatagrams(transport) {
  const reader = transport.datagrams.readable.getReader();
  while (true) {
    const { value, done } = await reader.read();
    if (done) break;
    processDatagram(value);
  }
}
```

Receiving server-initiated streams:
```javascript
async function acceptStreams(transport) {
  const reader = transport.incomingBidirectionalStreams.getReader();
  while (true) {
    const { value: stream, done } = await reader.read();
    if (done) break;
    handleStream(stream);
  }
}
```

WebTransport advantage over WebSocket: multiplexed streams avoid head-of-line blocking, datagrams support game/video use cases requiring speed over reliability.

