The Web Locks API provides mutex/reader-writer locks scoped to an origin. Prevents race conditions when multiple tabs or workers access shared resources like IndexedDB or localStorage.

Basic exclusive lock (default mode):
```javascript
// Only one tab/worker can hold 'my-resource' at a time
await navigator.locks.request('my-resource', async (lock) => {
  await readModifyWrite(); // safe — no concurrent access
}); // lock automatically released when callback resolves
```

Shared lock (multiple readers, no writers):
```javascript
// Multiple tabs can hold shared lock simultaneously
await navigator.locks.request('data-store', { mode: 'shared' }, async (lock) => {
  const data = await readData();
  return data;
});

// Exclusive lock blocks until all shared locks released
await navigator.locks.request('data-store', { mode: 'exclusive' }, async (lock) => {
  await writeData(newData);
});
```

Leader election across tabs:
```javascript
navigator.locks.request('leader', { steal: false }, async (lock) => {
  console.log('This tab is the leader — syncing data');
  while (true) {
    await syncWithServer();
    await sleep(30000);
  }
  // Other tabs wait in queue — next tab becomes leader when this one closes
});
```

With timeout via AbortSignal:
```javascript
async function tryAcquireLock(name, timeoutMs) {
  const controller = new AbortController();
  const timeout = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), timeoutMs);
  try {
    return await navigator.locks.request(name, { signal: controller.signal }, async () => {
      clearTimeout(timeout);
      return await doWork();
    });
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.name === 'AbortError') throw new Error('Lock timeout');
    throw err;
  }
}
```

Check if lock available without waiting:
```javascript
await navigator.locks.request('resource', { ifAvailable: true }, async (lock) => {
  if (!lock) { console.log('Busy — try later'); return; }
  await doWork();
});
```

Query current lock state (debug):
```javascript
const state = await navigator.locks.query();
console.log('Held:', state.held);
console.log('Pending:', state.pending);
```

Deadlock prevention: avoid nested lock requests. If two tabs each request [A, B] and [B, A], circular wait causes deadlock. Always acquire locks in consistent order.

