Symbol.asyncIterator defines the async iteration protocol. Objects with [Symbol.asyncIterator]() method can be used in for-await-of loops, enabling pull-based consumption of async data streams.

Basic async iterable:
```javascript
const myAsyncIterable = {
  async *[Symbol.asyncIterator]() {
    yield 'hello';
    yield 'async';
    yield 'iteration';
  }
};

for await (const word of myAsyncIterable) {
  console.log(word); // hello, async, iteration
}
```

Timed data source (simulates real async stream):
```javascript
const timedSource = {
  delays: [200, 500, 1000],

  async *[Symbol.asyncIterator]() {
    for (const delay of this.delays) {
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, delay));
      yield `Data after ${delay}ms`;
    }
  }
};

for await (const item of timedSource) {
  console.log(item);
}
```

Class-based async iterable (e.g., paginated API):
```javascript
class PaginatedAPI {
  constructor(endpoint) {
    this.endpoint = endpoint;
  }

  async *[Symbol.asyncIterator]() {
    let page = 1;
    while (true) {
      const res = await fetch(`${this.endpoint}?page=${page}`);
      const data = await res.json();
      if (data.items.length === 0) return; // done
      yield* data.items;
      if (!data.hasNextPage) return;
      page++;
    }
  }
}

const api = new PaginatedAPI('/api/users');
for await (const user of api) {
  processUser(user);
}
```

Async iterable with cleanup (return method):
```javascript
function createEventStream(emitter, event) {
  return {
    [Symbol.asyncIterator]() {
      const queue = [];
      let resolve = null;
      const handler = (data) => {
        if (resolve) { resolve({ value: data, done: false }); resolve = null; }
        else queue.push(data);
      };
      emitter.on(event, handler);
      return {
        next() {
          if (queue.length) return Promise.resolve({ value: queue.shift(), done: false });
          return new Promise(r => { resolve = r; });
        },
        return() {
          emitter.off(event, handler); // cleanup
          return Promise.resolve({ done: true });
        }
      };
    }
  };
}
```

