AbortSignal.any() combines multiple AbortSignals into one — the result aborts when ANY input signal aborts, using the first signal's abort reason. Enables complex cancellation logic without manual coordination.

Combining user cancel + timeout:
```javascript
async function fetchWithUserOrTimeout(url) {
  const userController = new AbortController();
  cancelButton.onclick = () => userController.abort('User cancelled');

  const combinedSignal = AbortSignal.any([
    userController.signal,
    AbortSignal.timeout(5000) // 5 second timeout
  ]);

  try {
    const response = await fetch(url, { signal: combinedSignal });
    return await response.json();
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.name === 'AbortError') {
      console.log('Aborted:', err.message); // reason from first abort
    }
    throw err;
  }
}
```

Three-way signal: user cancel + timeout + parent abort:
```javascript
function createChildSignal(parentSignal, timeoutMs) {
  return AbortSignal.any([
    parentSignal,
    AbortSignal.timeout(timeoutMs)
  ]);
}

async function processItem(item, parentSignal) {
  const signal = createChildSignal(parentSignal, 3000);
  const result = await fetch(`/api/items/${item.id}`, { signal });
  return result.json();
}

// Parent can abort all children at once
const parent = new AbortController();
const results = await Promise.all(
  items.map(item => processItem(item, parent.signal))
);
```

