**Scenario (E-commerce):** Implementing this pattern to handle products efficiently.

Long synchronous operations block the event loop — no I/O, timers, or user interactions can process until the sync work finishes. Fatal for responsive async applications.

Bad — blocking loop:
```javascript
app.get('/compute', async (req, res) => {
  // Blocks event loop for entire duration — all other requests stall
  let result = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < 1_000_000_000; i++) {
    result += Math.sqrt(i);
  }
  res.json({ result });
});
```

Fix option 1 — Worker Thread for CPU-bound work:
```javascript
const { Worker } = require('worker_threads');

function computeInWorker(n) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const worker = new Worker(`
      const { parentPort, workerData } = require('worker_threads');
      let result = 0;
