Scheduler.postTask() schedules tasks with explicit priorities — user-blocking, user-visible, or background. Enables cooperative multitasking without blocking the event loop.

Three priority levels:
- user-blocking: highest, critical UI work
- user-visible: default, normal user-facing tasks
- background: lowest, non-urgent work

Basic usage:
```javascript
// Schedule background work — won't compete with UI
await scheduler.postTask(() => {
  processAnalytics(data);
}, { priority: 'background' });

// User-blocking: runs before normal tasks
await scheduler.postTask(() => {
  updateCriticalUI();
}, { priority: 'user-blocking' });
```

With delay:
```javascript
await scheduler.postTask(() => prefetchData(), { delay: 2000 });
```

Dynamic priority via TaskController:
```javascript
const controller = new TaskController({ priority: 'user-visible' });
const task = scheduler.postTask(doWork, { signal: controller.signal });

// Downgrade priority if user navigates away
controller.setPriority('background');

// Or abort
controller.abort();
task.catch(err => console.log('Task aborted:', err.name));
```

Priority scheduling pattern — batching work by priority:
```javascript
const tasks = [
  { work: saveUserInput, priority: 'user-blocking' },
  { work: updateSidebar, priority: 'user-visible' },
  { work: logAnalytics, priority: 'background' },
  { work: prefetchImages, priority: 'background' },
];

// All scheduled — browser runs in priority order
const results = await Promise.all(
  tasks.map(({ work, priority }) =>
    scheduler.postTask(work, { priority })
  )
);
```

Feature detect before use:
```javascript
if ('scheduler' in globalThis && 'postTask' in scheduler) {
  await scheduler.postTask(work, { priority: 'background' });
} else {
  setTimeout(work, 0); // fallback
}
```

Note: Limited browser availability — not yet Baseline. Check support before production use.

