requestIdleCallback runs work only when the browser is idle — no pending rendering, no user input processing. Prevents background tasks from competing with critical work.

Basic pattern:
```javascript
function runWhenIdle(tasks) {
  requestIdleCallback((deadline) => {
    while (deadline.timeRemaining() > 1 && tasks.length > 0) {
      const task = tasks.shift();
      task();
    }
    if (tasks.length > 0) {
      requestIdleCallback(runWhenIdle.bind(null, tasks)); // reschedule remaining
    }
  });
}

const lowPriorityWork = [
  () => preloadImages(nextPageImages),
  () => cleanupOldCache(),
  () => buildSearchIndex(content),
];
runWhenIdle(lowPriorityWork);
```

timeRemaining() — check available time:
```javascript
requestIdleCallback((deadline) => {
  console.log(`Idle time remaining: ${deadline.timeRemaining()}ms`);
  // Do as much work as time allows
  while (deadline.timeRemaining() > 5) {
    const chunk = getNextWorkChunk();
    if (!chunk) break;
    processChunk(chunk);
  }
});
```

With timeout (guarantee execution even if never truly idle):
```javascript
requestIdleCallback((deadline) => {
  if (deadline.didTimeout) {
    // Timeout fired — must do critical cleanup now even if not idle
    emergencyCleanup();
  } else {
    normalBackgroundWork(deadline);
  }
}, { timeout: 5000 }); // run within 5s regardless
```

Cancel idle callback:
```javascript
const callbackId = requestIdleCallback(myCallback);
// Cancel if conditions change
if (userNavigated) {
  cancelIdleCallback(callbackId);
}
```

Safe pattern with feature detection:
```javascript
const scheduleIdle = typeof requestIdleCallback !== 'undefined'
  ? requestIdleCallback
  : (fn) => setTimeout(fn, 1); // Safari fallback
```

Use for: preloading, cache cleanup, analytics, search index building, prefetching. NOT for: user-visible updates, time-sensitive operations.

