for-await-of iterates async iterables, automatically awaiting each yielded value. Works in async functions and module top-level. Also works with sync iterables, awaiting each value.

Basic usage with async generator:
```javascript
async function* source() {
  yield 1;
  yield Promise.resolve(2);
  yield 3;
}

async function consume() {
  for await (const val of source()) {
    console.log(val); // 1, 2, 3
  }
}
```

With fetch stream (ReadableStream):
```javascript
async function processStream(url) {
  const res = await fetch(url);
  for await (const chunk of res.body) {
    const text = new TextDecoder().decode(chunk);
    appendToOutput(text);
  }
}
```

Break early — triggers iterator cleanup via return():
```javascript
async function firstMatching(iterable, predicate) {
  for await (const item of iterable) {
    if (predicate(item)) return item; // break triggers cleanup
  }
  return null;
}
```

Error handling — catch rejects from yielded promises:
```javascript
async function safeIterate(iterable) {
  try {
    for await (const item of iterable) {
      processItem(item);
    }
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Iterator threw:', err);
  } finally {
    console.log('Iteration complete or errored');
  }
}
```

Sync iterable in for-await (awaits each value):
```javascript
function* syncWithPromises() {
  yield 'immediate';
  yield fetch('/api/slow').then(r => r.text()); // promise yielded
}

for await (const val of syncWithPromises()) {
  console.log(val); // awaits the fetch promise automatically
}
```

Caution — sync generator yielding rejected promise skips finally:
```javascript
// Avoid yielding rejected promises from sync generators inside for-await
// Use async generator instead to handle errors properly
async function* safeSource() {
  try {
    yield await riskyOperation();
  } catch (err) {
    // handle here — don't let rejection propagate to for-await caller
  }
}
```

