MessageChannel creates a pair of MessagePorts for direct point-to-point communication. Unlike postMessage to worker.onmessage, MessageChannel enables direct two-way channels between workers, or between workers bypassing the main thread.

Basic channel setup:
```javascript
const channel = new MessageChannel();
// port1 stays here, port2 transferred to worker
channel.port1.onmessage = (e) => console.log('Reply:', e.data);

const worker = new Worker('worker.js');
worker.postMessage({ port: channel.port2 }, [channel.port2]); // transfer port2

// Send via channel
channel.port1.postMessage({ cmd: 'process', data: payload });
```

Worker side:
```javascript
// worker.js
self.onmessage = (e) => {
  const port = e.data.port;
  port.onmessage = async (msg) => {
    const result = await processData(msg.data.data);
    port.postMessage({ result }); // reply directly on port
  };
};
```

Worker-to-worker direct channel (no main thread relay):
```javascript
// Main thread orchestrates initial handshake
const channel = new MessageChannel();
const worker1 = new Worker('worker1.js');
const worker2 = new Worker('worker2.js');

// Give each worker one port — they communicate directly
worker1.postMessage({ peer: channel.port1 }, [channel.port1]);
worker2.postMessage({ peer: channel.port2 }, [channel.port2]);

// Now worker1 and worker2 talk directly — main thread not involved
```

Request-response over channel:
```javascript
function createRPC(port) {
  const pending = new Map();
  let nextId = 0;

  port.onmessage = (e) => {
    const { id, result, error } = e.data;
    const { resolve, reject } = pending.get(id);
    pending.delete(id);
    error ? reject(new Error(error)) : resolve(result);
  };

  return {
    call(method, args) {
      const id = nextId++;
      const promise = new Promise((resolve, reject) => pending.set(id, { resolve, reject }));
      port.postMessage({ id, method, args });
      return promise;
    }
  };
}

const rpc = createRPC(channel.port1);
const result = await rpc.call('compute', { n: 1000000 });
```

