Service Workers run in a separate thread, intercept network requests, and can run background tasks even when the page is closed. Key patterns for offline-first and background sync.

Install and cache assets:
```javascript
// service-worker.js
const CACHE = 'app-v1';
const PRECACHE = ['/index.html', '/app.js', '/styles.css'];

self.addEventListener('install', (event) => {
  event.waitUntil(
    caches.open(CACHE).then(cache => cache.addAll(PRECACHE))
  );
});
```

Fetch interception — cache-first strategy:
```javascript
self.addEventListener('fetch', (event) => {
  event.respondWith(
    caches.match(event.request).then(cached => {
      if (cached) return cached; // cache hit
      return fetch(event.request).then(response => {
        // Cache successful responses
        if (response.status === 200) {
          const clone = response.clone();
          caches.open(CACHE).then(cache => cache.put(event.request, clone));
        }
        return response;
      });
    })
  );
});
```

Stale-while-revalidate strategy:
```javascript
self.addEventListener('fetch', (event) => {
  event.respondWith(
    caches.open(CACHE).then(async (cache) => {
      const cached = await cache.match(event.request);
      const networkPromise = fetch(event.request).then(response => {
        cache.put(event.request, response.clone()); // update cache in background
        return response;
      });
      return cached || networkPromise; // return cached immediately, update async
    })
  );
});
```

