ResizeObserver reports element dimension changes asynchronously before paint. Avoids polling with setInterval for responsive components.

Basic usage:
```javascript
const observer = new ResizeObserver((entries) => {
  for (const entry of entries) {
    const { inlineSize: width, blockSize: height } = entry.contentBoxSize[0];
    console.log(`Element resized: ${width}px x ${height}px`);
    updateLayout(entry.target, width, height);
  }
});

observer.observe(container);
// observer.unobserve(container); // stop one
// observer.disconnect();          // stop all
```

Responsive component (different views at different widths):
```javascript
const chartObserver = new ResizeObserver((entries) => {
  for (const entry of entries) {
    const width = entry.contentBoxSize[0].inlineSize;
    const chart = entry.target._chartInstance;
    if (width < 400) chart.setCompactMode(true);
    else chart.setCompactMode(false);
    chart.resize(width);
  }
});

chartObserver.observe(chartContainer);
```

Avoiding infinite resize loops:
```javascript
// BAD — modifying size in callback triggers new observation → infinite loop
const bad = new ResizeObserver((entries) => {
  entries[0].target.style.height = entries[0].contentBoxSize[0].inlineSize + 'px';
  // triggers another resize → another callback → loop!
});

// GOOD — defer mutation to next frame
const good = new ResizeObserver((entries) => {
  requestAnimationFrame(() => {
    for (const entry of entries) {
      entry.target.style.height = entry.contentBoxSize[0].inlineSize + 'px';
    }
  });
});
```

Entry properties:
- contentBoxSize: [{inlineSize, blockSize}] — content area (excludes padding/border)
- borderBoxSize: [{inlineSize, blockSize}] — includes padding+border
- devicePixelContentBoxSize: physical pixels (for canvas rendering)
- contentRect: legacy DOMRectReadOnly (use contentBoxSize instead)

