**Scenario (Gaming):** Implementing this pattern to handle players efficiently.

When a cache entry is invalidated, multiple concurrent readers may simultaneously find the cache cold and all fetch fresh data — cache stampede. Or a stale reader may overwrite a fresh cache entry.

Bug — stale write overwrites fresh data:
```javascript
const cache = new Map();

async function getCachedUser(id) {
  if (cache.has(id)) return cache.get(id);

  const user = await fetchUser(id); // concurrent calls all fetch
  cache.set(id, user); // last write wins — may overwrite newer data
  return user;
}

// Invalidation race:
async function updateUser(id, data) {
  await saveUser(id, data);  // update DB
  cache.delete(id);           // invalidate
  // But a concurrent getCachedUser already started fetching old data
  // and will cache the stale result AFTER invalidation!
}
```

Fix — version-tagged cache entries:
```javascript
const cache = new Map(); // Map<id, {version, data}>
let cacheVersion = 0;

async function getUser(id) {
  const entry = cache.get(id);
  if (entry && entry.version === cacheVersion) return entry.data;

  const snapshotVersion = cacheVersion;
  const user = await fetchUser(id);

  // Only cache if version hasn't changed since we started fetching
  if (cacheVersion === snapshotVersion) {
    cache.set(id, { version: cacheVersion, data: user });
  }
  return user;
}

async function updateUser(id, data) {
  await saveUser(id, data);
  cacheVersion++; // bump version — all cached entries become stale
}
```

