Service Workers must never block their event handling — synchronous operations, infinite loops, or missing event.waitUntil() cause the SW to terminate early or miss events.

Bad — synchronous blocking in SW:
```javascript
self.addEventListener('fetch', (event) => {
  // NEVER do this — blocks SW thread
  const cache = caches.open('app'); // returns a promise — this does nothing useful
  const response = cache.match(event.request); // also a promise!
  event.respondWith(response); // responding with a promise — accidentally correct
  // But any sync computation here blocks all fetch handling
  for (let i = 0; i < 1e9; i++) {} // kills SW responsiveness
});
```

Bad — missing waitUntil in install:
```javascript
self.addEventListener('install', (event) => {
  // Without waitUntil — SW activates before cache is ready!
  caches.open('v1').then(cache => cache.addAll(PRECACHE));
  // install event completes immediately — cache may not be populated
});
```

Good — always use waitUntil and respondWith with Promises:
```javascript
self.addEventListener('install', (event) => {
  event.waitUntil( // tells SW to wait for this promise before completing install
    caches.open('v1').then(cache => cache.addAll(PRECACHE))
  );
});

self.addEventListener('fetch', (event) => {
  event.respondWith( // promise — SW waits for this to resolve
    caches.match(event.request).then(cached => {
      return cached || fetch(event.request);
    })
  );
});

self.addEventListener('activate', (event) => {
  event.waitUntil(
    caches.keys().then(keys =>
      Promise.all(keys.filter(k => k !== 'v1').map(k => caches.delete(k)))
    )
  );
});
```

